    "blurb": "Jerry’s birthday night shines on an electrifying Dark Star → El Paso → Eyes Of The World → Morning Dew suite. The second set maintains the momentum with tight rhythm work and standout vocal moments. Overall, a high‑octane performance captured in several excellent soundboard recordings.",
    "review": "On August 1, 1973 at Roosevelt Stadium the Dead celebrated Jerry’s birthday with an inspired two‑set marathon that still feels fresh today. The first set rolls through solid roots numbers before handing off to a second‑set powerhouse: a seamless Dark Star > El Paso > Eyes Of The World > Morning Dew sequence that showcases Jerry’s soaring lead, Phil’s funky, driving bass and Bill’s punchy drums, all underpinned by Keith’s tasteful piano accents. Highlights like Big River and the emotive vocal delivery on Me & My Uncle and Sugar Magnolia add extra color, while occasional mix quirks on Bird Song don’t detract from the overall excitement. With crisp soundboard tapes that capture both the band’s tight interplay and the stadium ambience, this birthday gig stands out as a must‑listen snapshot of the early‑’70s Dead in top form.",
